30:**Main chip and radio (sheet 2).** Unchanged from A3. U1 nRF54LM20A CAAA, copied pin by pin from Nordic's CAAA reference schematic, configuration 1: VDD balls A4 and E10 on VDD_1V8 with C4, C5, C1, C2; DCC (A5) to L1 to DECD (A6) with C6; FB1 DECD to DECA (A8) and DECRF (B2) with C7, C14; DECUSB (H8) to C10 only; VBUS (H9) through R1 2.2 ohm with C11; TXRTUNE (G6) R2; X1 32 MHz, X2 32.768 kHz; antenna chain L2, C3, L3, C12, L4, C13 (not mounted), ANT1. Every signal ball of section 7 goes to its function; the 11 spare balls go to test pads; MIC_B_CLK (E6), MIC_B_DATA (D7) and JOY_CENTER (H4) go to test pads only (A5).
32:**Power (sheet 3).** U2 nPM1304 (A6, architecture 17.13) with the passives of the nPM1300 kit design C71 to C80, L71, L72, R71, R72, R57, R58, each marked in bom.csv 'to confirm against the nPM1304 product specification' (S18). A7: U2 is nPM1304-CAAA-R7 with its 35 real balls (Table 33, page 153; section 12); C71 is 1.0 uF 25 V, C85, C86, C87, C88 are added (npm1304-reference.md D1 to D4). The cell BT1 and the thermistor RT1 moved to the band sheet (section 17.3): the nets VBAT and NTC reach them through J_BAND_B. SHPHLD to test pad TP19. CC1, CC2, GPIO1 to GPIO3, LED0 to LED2 are no-connect (A7: GPIO4 does not exist on the package).
34:**Microphones (sheet 4).** A7: U5 and U6 Knowles SPK0641HT4H-1 (pins 1 DATA, 2 CLOCK, 3 SELECT, 4 Vdd, 5 to 8 GROUND, Knowles sheet 6; all four GROUND pins on ground). Was: IM68D128B with provisional P1 to P5. Both CLOCK on MIC_A_CLK (F1); DATA of each through its own 100 ohm (R31, R32) to MIC_A_DATA (F2); SELECT of U5 on ground, of U6 on VDD_MIC; each has 1 uF (C31, C32) and 100 nF (C35, C36) from VDD_MIC to ground.
36:**Storage (sheet 5).** U3 CSNP32GCR01-BOW, pads numbered as the maker table (spec V1.0 p5, section 2.1): 1 DAT2, 2 DAT3 = SDC_CS, 3 CLK = SDC_SCK, 4 VSS, 5 CMD = SDC_MOSI, 6 DAT0 = SDC_MISO, 7 DAT1, 8 VCC = VDD_SD. A6: the four bus lines no longer join the chip balls directly: U10 (SN74AXC4T774RSVR) carries SD_SCK (A9), SD_MOSI (B10), SD_CS (D9) from the 1.8 V side to the card side nets SDC_SCK, SDC_MOSI, SDC_CS and SDC_MISO back to SD_MISO (D10); see section 11, F07. 47 kohm pull-ups to VDD_SD on DAT0 (R60 on SDC_MISO), DAT1 (R63), DAT2 (R64), DAT3/CS (R65 on SDC_CS); C60 4.7 uF and C61 100 nF on VDD_SD (W3).
